.. csv-table::
   :header: "Event", "Example"
   :widths: 30, 20

   "
   ``<taskname>#ID``
   A finger was scanned. ``%eventvalue1%`` is the slot of the recognized finger, or ``-1`` when it was not recognized. Sent once per touch, together with the ``Score`` and ``Count`` values.
   ","

   .. code-block:: none

      on Finger#ID do
        if %eventvalue1% >= 0
          Pulse,26,1,2000
        endif
      endon

   "
   "
   ``<taskname>#EnrollScan=<n>``
   Enrollment: place the finger on the sensor, capture ``<n>`` = 1 or 2.
   ","

   .. code-block:: none

      on Finger#EnrollScan do
        LogEntry,'Place the finger (%eventvalue1%/2)'
      endon

   "
   "
   ``<taskname>#EnrollRemove=<n>``
   Enrollment: lift the finger after capture ``<n>``.
   ","

   .. code-block:: none

      on Finger#EnrollRemove do
        LogEntry,'Lift the finger'
      endon

   "
   "
   ``<taskname>#Enrolled=<id>``
   Enrollment done, the finger is stored at slot ``<id>``.
   ","

   .. code-block:: none

      on Finger#Enrolled do
        LogEntry,'Finger stored at %eventvalue1%'
      endon

   "
   "
   ``<taskname>#EnrollFailed=<code>``
   Enrollment failed, see the error codes.
   ","

   .. code-block:: none

      on Finger#EnrollFailed do
        LogEntry,'Enrollment failed, code %eventvalue1%'
      endon

   "
   "
   ``<taskname>#Deleted=<id>``
   Slot ``<id>`` deleted by ``fingerprint,delete``, or ``-1`` after ``fingerprint,deleteall``.
   ","
   "
   "
   ``<taskname>#Count=<n>``
   Answer to ``fingerprint,count``: ``<n>`` fingers are stored in the module.
   ","
   "
   "
   ``<taskname>#Error=<code>``
   ``fingerprint,delete``, ``deleteall``, ``count`` or ``led`` failed, see the error codes.
   ","
   "

These events are only generated when Rules are enabled.
